The agent-facing tree is authored, not vendored, so there is no upstream conversion table to
keep. What the short names in /app/kv mean, for the author's own reference:

  kv/          the token cache this service manages
  pool.py      the pool of pages: free, reusable, held, and the take-back
  keep.py      the reuse index and the walk from the start of a prompt
  live.py      residency - which pages a request is holding right now
  fill.py      the filling of a prompt, chunk by chunk
  turn.py      one scheduling step
  put.py       writing one token, and completing a page
  store.py     the frozen records: a page, a request, and the trace
  ops.py       the program language
  run_kv.py    the driver

  rq.prompt    the prompt tokens of a request
  rq.out       the tokens it will emit, one per decode
  rq.fed       how many prompt tokens are placed
  rq.made      how many tokens it has emitted
  rq.pg        the pages it holds now, by page slot
  rq.up        the lowest page outside the sink it still holds
  kv.n w a s b pool size, page width, sink tokens, window tokens, step budget
  kv.fr        free page numbers
  kv.ref       holders per page
  kv.use       reusable pages, oldest release first
  kv.ix        the reuse index
  kv.kid       the pages below each page
  kv.ok        whether a walk can still reach a page
